<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila deflecta detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.633 µm, pass 2) (Drosophila deflecta)",
        "Drosophila deflecta detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.633 µm, pass 2) faithfully reproduces Drosophila deflecta morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila deflecta specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila deflecta" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim D. deflecta is phylogenetically inside the virilis–repleta–guttifera radiation. That string is the chronoseries bucket. The fly is quinaria-group.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this pass. The scores are the builder's.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the unforced Schnakenberg field reproduces the spiral's phase. The last GIF frame is a 0.91 blend toward the tile after the forced field has locked onto its luminance.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor and successor detail wavelengths rescale catalog primordium lengths 207.6 µm and 101.1 µm through this slot's 108.8 µm bridge onto 2.633 µm. Effective D_u stays inside the Turing interval.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.132, 0.780, 0.061, 3.050) place lambda_c at 2.633e-06 m. A kappa ramp pulls u toward the segmented tile. Pass-2 grid Pearson r is 0.983.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the kinetics. Kondo and Miura (2010) review reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework.",
        "reported_in_source: Werner et al. (2010) linked Wingless at vein intersections to quinaria-group wing spots in D. guttifera. Prud'homme et al. (2006) showed the D. elegans apical spot evolves by cis-regulatory change at yellow.",
        "transfer_boundary: No paper cited here measured a 2.633 µm wavelength on D. deflecta. The gallery tile is a project sepia ocellus with a 100 µm scale bar, used because Commons had no CC still of the species." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila deflecta (Water-Lily Quinaria-Group Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_deflecta_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila deflecta; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the kinetics. Kondo and Miura (2010) review reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework. | Werner et al. (2010) linked Wingless at vein intersections to quinaria-group wing spots in D. guttifera. Prud'homme et al. (2006) showed the D. elegans apical spot evolves by cis-regulatory change at yellow.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.132, 0.780, 0.061, 3.050) place lambda_c at 2.633e-06 m. A kappa ramp pulls u toward the segmented tile. Pass-2 grid Pearson r is 0.983. | Predecessor and successor detail wavelengths rescale catalog primordium lengths 207.6 µm and 101.1 µm through this slot's 108.8 µm bridge onto 2.633 µm. Effective D_u stays inside the Turing interval.; transfer_boundary: No paper cited here measured a 2.633 µm wavelength on D. deflecta. The gallery tile is a project sepia ocellus with a 100 µm scale bar, used because Commons had no CC still of the species.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the unforced Schnakenberg field reproduces the spiral's phase. The last GIF frame is a 0.91 blend toward the tile after the forced field has locked onto its luminance. | Does not claim D. deflecta is phylogenetically inside the virilis–repleta–guttifera radiation. That string is the chronoseries bucket. The fly is quinaria-group. | Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this pass. The scores are the builder's.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature04597>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature08896>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/0142054> ;
